Application Control names the application behind each connection with
the open nDPI library (OPNsense's package ndpi), and keeps the servers
it names in pf tables: one for every category nDPI knows and one for
each application chosen, each an External alias in Firewall: Aliases
for rules to use, with an expiry. It reads a copy of the traffic of the
internal interfaces (tcpdump -p, no port made promiscuous) and stands
in no connection's way. A connection named only by its port or address
is shown as a guess and put in no table; those nDPI does not name are
listed with the server name and the JA4 fingerprint their TLS client
sent. On by default. Nothing is blocked yet.

